# Design system rules (non-negotiable, §11.6)

Three rules, lint-enforced and reviewed in every PR.

## Rule 1 — Semantic components exist before pages

Pages compose semantic components from `packages/ui/src/semantic/*`. They never reach for primitives directly. Examples: `<ClientCard>`, `<PhasePill>`, `<DataTable>`, `<FactFindFieldGroup>`, `<WizardStepHeader>`, `<EmptyState>`, `<RoleBadge>`, `<PortalKanban>`.

## Rule 2 — Never style inside pages or features

Files under `apps/web/src/app/routes/**` and `apps/web/src/features/**` MUST NOT contain Tailwind utility classes for visual styling, inline `style={}`, `styled-components`, or CSS Module class lists. Their only styling responsibility is **layout composition** via primitives (`<PageShell>`, `<Stack>`, `<Cluster>`, `<Grid>`, `<Inline>`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — styling in a route/feature file
<div className="bg-white rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
  <h1 className="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Clients</h1>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — pure composition, semantic component owns the visuals
<PageShell title="Clients">
  <PortalKanban>...</PortalKanban>
</PageShell>
```

## Rule 3 — Tokens are the only source of visual values

No raw hex colours, no raw `px`/`rem` values outside `packages/ui/src/tokens/`. All visual values resolve through the token API (`tokens.color.brandPrimary`, `tokens.space.cardPadding`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div style={{ backgroundColor: '#3B82F6', padding: '16px' }} />

// ✅ GOOD — semantic component consumes tokens internally
<Card>...</Card>
```

## Layering (lower layers never import from higher)

```
Layer 0  Tokens          packages/ui/src/tokens/*
Layer 1  Primitives      Box, Stack, Cluster, Grid, Inline (layout only)
Layer 2  Atoms           Button, Input, Checkbox, Tag, Pill, Avatar, Icon
Layer 3  Molecules       FormField, Tabs, Combobox, DatePicker, MoneyField
Layer 4  Semantic        AppShell, Card, DataTable, PhasePill, ClientCard, …
Layer 5  Features        apps/web/src/features/**     (no styling)
Layer 6  Routes          apps/web/src/app/routes/**   (composition + data)
```

## Wrap third-party UI; never import directly from features

- `lucide-react` — never imported in feature/route code. Use `<Icon name="..." />` from Layer 2.
- `shadcn/ui` — always wrapped by a semantic component before pages use it.
- Brand colours come from the resolved tenant brand bundle via `<BrandThemeProvider>` (CSS variables on `:root`). Never hard-code a tenant colour.

## Tailwind version + token plumbing

- The workspace runs **Tailwind CSS v4** (PostCSS plugin: `@tailwindcss/postcss`). The web app entry CSS is `apps/web/src/styles/index.css`; it imports the canonical token sheet from `@advicelink/ui/styles.css`, then `@import "tailwindcss";`.
- The legacy v3 token preset (`packages/ui/src/tokens/tailwindPreset.ts` + `apps/web/tailwind.config.ts`) is kept and bridged into v4 via the `@config '../../tailwind.config.ts';` directive. This is the official v4 migration shim.
- New design tokens go into the `@theme` block in `packages/ui/src/styles/tokens.css` (NOT into the v3 preset). Token names follow v4 namespaces: `--color-*`, `--spacing-*`, `--font-*`, `--font-weight-*`, `--text-*`, `--radius-*`, `--shadow-*`. `@theme` may not be wrapped in a `@layer` import.
- shadcn install path:
  1. `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest init` from `packages/ui` — **never** from `apps/web` (would land files in a feature-layer location and violate Rules 1 + 2 above).
  2. Components land in `packages/ui/src/atoms/<name>/`. Wrap each in a Layer-4 semantic before any feature/route consumes it.
  3. shadcn-required CSS variables (e.g. `--sidebar-background`, `--primary`, `--muted-foreground`) live in the `@theme` block in `packages/ui/src/styles/tokens.css`. Bind them to the runtime brand vars (`--ui-color-brand-*`) so per-tenant theming still flows through `<BrandThemeProvider>`.
  4. The shadcn skill is installed at `.agents/skills/shadcn/SKILL.md`; consult it for `data-icon`, `cn()`, `FieldGroup`/`Field`, base-vs-radix, and overlay rules.

## Storybook is the source of visual truth

Every Layer 1–4 component has stories with controls and a Chromatic baseline. PR-time visual regression must be approved before merge. Stories run with a "Theme switcher" that flips between three example tenant brand bundles.
